      "title": "Gasoline Price (per gallon)",
      "description": "Average retail price per gallon of regular unleaded gasoline across U.S. cities, collected monthly by the BLS. Gas prices are one of the most visible and psychologically impactful costs in daily life - they affect not just your commute but also the price of shipped goods, groceries, and services. They're heavily influenced by crude oil prices, refinery capacity, seasonal blending requirements, and geopolitical events. A sharp spike here often foreshadows broader inflation a few months later.",
