      "title": "Egg Prices (per dozen)",
      "description": "Average retail price per dozen Grade A large eggs, collected monthly by the BLS. Eggs have become a cultural bellwether for food inflation - cheap to produce in stable times, but extremely volatile when supply chains are disrupted. The dramatic spikes you'll see in recent years are largely driven by avian flu outbreaks that wiped out millions of laying hens, sharply reducing supply. Egg prices are a good proxy for how stressed the food supply chain is at any given moment.",
