      "id": 5,
      "title": "Beef Prices (per lb)",
      "description": "Average retail price per pound of uncooked ground beef (all types), collected monthly by the BLS. Beef is one of the pricier staples in an American grocery cart, and its price reflects the full cost of the agricultural supply chain - feed costs, fuel for transport, labor at processing plants, and retail markups. It tends to rise with general inflation but can spike independently during drought years (which reduce cattle herd sizes) or supply chain disruptions. A long-term upward trend here means your grocery bill is quietly growing.",
